Z||000025||batboy||06-02-2000||01:05 PM||||Fierocious, the only thing I know for sure about dissimilar metals stuff is how to spell it and that it can cause corrosion. I think you're hinting at a very good point. A steel brace (I was planning on running on the radiator side of the front compartment) attached to an aluminum box might not be a great idea unless I figure out a way to isolate it using small rubber or nylon bushings. Probably aluminum isn't used because if it grounds against the positive terminal, it will start welding and melting the aluminum causing all kinds of problems. By the way, aluminum does eventually corrode, just not as quickly or as bad as iron or steel.||||reg||1
